RQ2: Logistic regression interpretation
The model predicts whether a fatal crash occurred on a weekend rather than a weekday using hour of day.

Midnight was the reference hour; all other hours were compared with midnight.

Crashes between 1 a.m. and 3 a.m. had higher odds of occurring on weekends.

At 2 a.m., fatal crashes had approximately 1.45 times the odds of occurring on a weekend rather than a weekday, compared with midnight crashes.

Crashes during most morning, afternoon, and evening hours had lower odds of occurring on weekends than crashes at midnight.

